# EXAMPLE / TEMPLATE — documentation only. NOT referenced in kustomization.yaml,
# so ArgoCD does NOT apply it. The real secret lives in alertmanager-config.sops.yaml,
# which is sops-encrypted — its stringData is an opaque ENC[] blob, so anyone cloning
# the repo to deploy their own cluster cannot see what to put inside. This file shows
# the cleartext structure.
#
# To create your own encrypted secret from this template:
#   1. cp alertmanager-config.sops.yaml.example alertmanager-config.sops.yaml
#   2. sops --encrypt --in-place alertmanager-config.sops.yaml
#      (gitops/.sops.yaml creation rule encrypts stringData with the age recipient
#      for any *.sops.yaml file; you need the matching age PRIVATE key to decrypt)
#   3. sops edit alertmanager-config.sops.yaml
#      fill the two placeholders (bot_token + chat_id), save -> re-encrypted + MAC
#   4. ensure `- alertmanager-config.sops.yaml` is listed under kustomization.yaml
#      resources (it already is in this repo)
#
# This SopsSecret (kind addons.projectcapsule.dev/v1alpha1, same CRD as the
# cert-manager/external-dns/ceph sops secrets) materializes Secret `alertmanager-config`
# (key alertmanager.yaml) in `monitoring`, which kube-prometheus-stack mounts via
# alertmanager.alertmanagerSpec.useExistingSecret + configSecret (see kps-values.yaml).
# It keeps the Telegram bot token out of plaintext helm values.
#
# NOTE — prometheus-operator strict validation: the operator validates this config
# during reconcile. chat_id MUST be non-zero (0 is rejected as "missing chat_id",
# -> PrometheusOperatorSyncFailed). The placeholder 123456789 below is non-zero so
# the config validates; replace it with your real chat id. With route.receiver=telegram
# the alertmanager will attempt sends to Telegram every repeat_interval (4h) once a
# real bot_token is in place.
#
# How to obtain the Telegram credentials:
#   bot_token: create a bot with @BotFather -> you get "<bot_id>:<token>"
#   chat_id:   your numeric chat id (message @userinfobot, or for a group add the bot
#              and read the update from the Bot API). Integer, non-zero.
apiVersion: addons.projectcapsule.dev/v1alpha1
kind: SopsSecret
metadata:
  name: alertmanager-config
  namespace: monitoring
  annotations:
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "-1"
spec:
  secrets:
    - name: alertmanager-config
      stringData:
        alertmanager.yaml: |
          global:
            resolve_timeout: 5m
          route:
            group_by: ["alertname", "namespace"]
            group_wait: 30s
            group_interval: 5m
            repeat_interval: 4h
            receiver: telegram
          receivers:
            - name: "null"
            - name: telegram
              telegram_configs:
                - bot_token: "REPLACE_WITH_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"   # from @BotFather, format "<bot_id>:<token>"
                  chat_id: 123456789                              # your chat id (integer, non-zero; 0 is rejected)
                  send_resolved: true